;;; emdysi's rules for the tokenizer, applied after the ERG's
;;; (grammar/erg/rpp/tokenizer.rpp), before the input is split into tokens.
;;;
;;; A range of amounts with a currency sign on both ends: |£3,000-£5,000|,
;;; |$10-$20|. The ERG splits a range of numbers (|10-20|, its group #2)
;;; and a hyphen between a word and a currency sign (|$8-to-$9|), but not
;;; between a number and a currency sign.

!([0-9])[–-]([#$€¢£¥]) ?([0-9])	\1 – \2 \3

;;; An amount of money with a suffix for its order of magnitude: |£2bn|,
;;; |$1.4bn|, |€5m|, |$300k|, read as |£ 2 billion| and so on. Only after a
;;; currency sign: |5m| alone may be metres.

!([#$€¢£¥]) ?([0-9][0-9.,]*)bn([^a-zA-Z]|$)	\1 \2 billion\3
!([#$€¢£¥]) ?([0-9][0-9.,]*)m([^a-zA-Z]|$)	\1 \2 million\3
!([#$€¢£¥]) ?([0-9][0-9.,]*)k([^a-zA-Z]|$)	\1 \2 thousand\3
